.TH AUTHD 8 "September 2026" "authd" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
authd \- Peios PGSS Logon authority
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/sbin/authd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B authd
is the Peios authentication authority.  It accepts logon requests on
.IR /run/logon.sock ,
coordinates credential verification with registered principal sources on
.IR /run/psi.sock ,
and returns a KACS primary token and profile for an authenticated principal.
The same socket also lets any authenticated principal change its own
credential, relayed to the principal source that holds it; see
.BR passwd (1).
On the same socket authd ends a logon session on request: it sends every
process whose primary token belongs to the session SIGTERM, waits up to five
seconds, sends SIGKILL to what is left, and looks again, at most three times.
The kernel destroys the session when its last token goes.  A person may end
their own session; ending anyone else's needs the right granted by
.IR SessionEndSecurity ,
below.  SYSTEM's session, Anonymous's, and a service's are never ended.
Identity queries are served separately on
.IR /run/ident.sock .
.PP
The daemon does not verify credentials or launch sessions.  Principal sources
such as
.BR lpsd (8)
verify credentials, and clients such as
.BR login (1)
install granted tokens on themselves.
.PP
The service is normally started by peinit from the registry definition shipped
in
.IR /usr/share/regim/authd-service.reg .
It takes no command-line options.
.SH SECURITY
.B authd
runs at PeiosTcb integrity with SeCreateTokenPrivilege and SeTcbPrivilege.
Its executable must carry a valid Peios TCB PIP signature.  Machine logon
policy is read from
.IR Machine\eGeneric\eAuthn\ePolicy .
.PP
Who may end another principal's logon session is the SDDL descriptor in the
REG_SZ value
.I SessionEndSecurity
on that key, access-checked with the caller's token for right 0x1 and read on
every request.  Where it is absent, SYSTEM and Administrators may:
.IR O:SYG:SYD:(A;;0x1;;;SY)(A;;0x1;;;BA) .
A value that is present but unusable lets nobody, and is logged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/logon.sock
PGSS Logon client socket.  SYSTEM and Administrators may connect, and so may
every authenticated principal, to change its own credential and to end its
own session.  Reaching it does not permit originating a logon; that is
decided per peer.
.TP
.I /run/psi.sock
Principal Source Interface registration socket.
.TP
.I /run/ident.sock
Identity lookup socket.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/authd-policy.reg
Default machine authentication-policy seed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR login (1),
.BR lps (1),
.BR passwd (1),
.BR lpsd (8)
